, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9af242a9efebbb0a022e8c51d7b916f12e3ae0e5096b5f02009f9a7528e5aa04</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e4331f64a2d48cd870bb118f35ea9df850096acc54dc9953759edf12004f3dd</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks Arctic strategy amid growing power rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a531a321f72d166a54c67270a49c2462969604dbefe5286f05eccb5e8062ef6</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-a